For the past week and a half I've been struggling with my computer to get it to work.  The problem started with EQ locking up and grew to a point where I could only play for about 20 minutes before I would have to reboot.<P>I ended up re-installing the OS several times, the last time it was on a squeaky clean hard drive, I even went so far as to wipe the Master Boot Record.  <P>Now I finally have a system that seems stable (I have not had that much of a chance to test it yet, but I hope to tonight.) My problem is when I'm playing EQ and the Fog, Rain or Night comes around I can only see as far as my face, about a five foot radius around my character.  Imagin if he fell down with his arm straight out, that is how far I can see.  What gives?????<P>- I have the clipping plane extended out to the max.<BR>- I have cranked up the Gamma and that makes the fog, night, rain look brighter but does not improve the fog length.<BR>- It worked fine before I reinstalled the OS.<BR>- It works/looks fine if I log into my other computer.<BR>- As soon as daylight comes or the rain stops I can see normally.<BR>- I have installed the latest drivers for my video card and the latest version of Direct X.  (ATI's All-in-Wonder Raden)<P>This makes the game virtually unplayable for over half the time and is very frustrating.  Anyone have a clue?
